  It sounds like you stopped working to improve your defense and offense
at some point.  Try on every non-cursed piece of armor you find for
enchantment.  Wear as much armor as possible:  shirt, body armor, cloak,
helm, gloves, shield, boots.  Particularly test accessory armor for
enchantment as you'll probably see a lot more of it.  Buy divine
protection.  

  Improve your offense: Improve strength, weapon(s), weapon skill,
ranged attack, etc.  How best to do this generally depends on your
class.   
  
  Ranged attacks:  
    Rogues, Valks and Wizards should throw daggers early and often.
    Rangers should use the bow.
    Tourists should use their darts.
    Healers should throw darts.
    Samurai should use yumi and ya.

  Expert missile skill doubles the damage you do.  (Which is all that 
Grayswandir does.  And Grayswandir isn't guaranteed.)

  Missile weapons can doubly benefit from Expert skill.  First from the
+2 damage bonus.  Second from the mulitplier effect of firing multiple
missiles.

  All damage bonuses get multiplied:

    Strength damage bonus (up to +6)  (not with a bow, crossbow, sling)
    Skill damage bonus 
    enchantment damage bonus
    poison damage bonus (darts,shuriken, arrows, crossbow bolts only)
    Ring(s) of increase damage.

  Rogues average 2.5 times the damage with daggers.
  Rangers can average 2.5 times the damage with any missile weapon.
  Samurai with yumi and ya can get 2.5 times the damage.
  Elves/orcs at expert bow using racial bow/arrow get 2.5 times the 
    damage.
    


